# Shell scripts must keep LF endings whatever the checkout platform.
#
# A CRLF shebang makes the interpreter "not found" inside a Linux container --
# the script exists, is executable, and still fails. It cost one debugging cycle
# on the dashboard entrypoint; this makes it impossible to reintroduce by
# checking the repository out on Windows.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# The model artefact is committed (D-48) and its SHA-256 is verified at every
# startup. Declaring it binary is not decoration: git's text heuristic is a
# guess, and a single CRLF translation on a Windows checkout would change the
# digest and make the streaming job refuse to start -- on the reviewer's
# machine, never on ours.
*.joblib binary
